Relevant columns and their potential usage for copy‑number analyses  

• "project_short_name": filter to the breast‑cancer cohort (value ‘TCGA‑BRCA’).  
• "case_barcode": patient identifier; needed to aggregate CNVs per case.  
• "sample_barcode": tumour/normal sample identifier; used when choosing one sample per case.  
• "aliquot_barcode": unique aliquot identifier; distinguishes multiple CN segment sets for the same sample.  
• "chromosome": chromosome on which the segment lies; needed when mapping to cytobands.  
• "start_pos", "end_pos": genomic coordinates; used to measure overlap with a cytoband.  
• "segment_mean": log2‑ratio of copy number; the signal to be averaged (length‑weighted).  
• "num_probes": quality / weight information (optional).  
• "file_gdc_id": ties the record to the specific GDC Release 23 file (if further file level checks are required).  
• "case_gdc_id", "sample_gdc_id", "aliquot_gdc_id": UUIDs corresponding to the above barcodes; handy when barcodes are duplicated or truncated.

Typical conditions that can be applied  
1. "project_short_name" = 'TCGA‑BRCA'              -- restrict to breast cancer  
2. "chromosome" IN ('chr1', … , 'chrX')            -- focus on canonical chromosomes if necessary  
3. WHERE "segment_mean" IS NOT NULL                -- keep rows with CN values  
4. GROUP BY "case_barcode", "chromosome"           -- per‑patient summaries  
5. ORDER BY "start_pos"                            -- inspect genomic order  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progressively examine the data. Adjust the fully‑qualified names to match your environment exactly.

```sql
-- 1. Description: List all distinct TCGA projects represented in the copy‑number table.
SELECT DISTINCT "project_short_name"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show the different chromosome identifiers present in the dataset.
SELECT DISTINCT "chromosome"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
ORDER BY "chromosome"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: View a few breast‑cancer (TCGA‑BRCA) copy‑number segments.
SELECT *
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Count how many segments each breast‑cancer case contains.
SELECT "case_barcode",
       COUNT(*) AS "segment_count"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "case_barcode"
ORDER BY "segment_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Inspect the range of segment_mean values across BRCA samples.
SELECT MIN("segment_mean") AS "min_log2",
       MAX("segment_mean") AS "max_log2",
       AVG("segment_mean") AS "avg_log2"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Retrieve distinct tumour sample barcodes for BRCA.
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_barcode"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
ORDER BY "sample_barcode"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Average log2 copy‑number per chromosome per BRCA case.
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "chromosome",
       AVG("segment_mean") AS "mean_log2_chr"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "case_barcode", "chromosome"
ORDER BY "case_barcode", "chromosome"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Length‑weighted mean log2 CN per case (all chromosomes combined).
SELECT "case_barcode",
       SUM( ("end_pos" - "start_pos") * "segment_mean" ) / 
       NULLIF( SUM("end_pos" - "start_pos"), 0 ) AS "length_weighted_log2"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "case_barcode"
ORDER BY "length_weighted_log2"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Detect highly amplified segments in BRCA (log2 ratio > 1.5 ≈ >5 copies).
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "chromosome",
       "start_pos",
       "end_pos",
       "segment_mean"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "segment_mean" > 1.5
ORDER BY "segment_mean" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: For one sample, list all segments on chromosome 17 in genomic order.
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "sample_barcode",
       "start_pos",
       "end_pos",
       "segment_mean",
       "num_probes"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "chromosome" = '17'
  AND "sample_barcode" = (  -- pick an arbitrary sample to inspect
        SELECT DISTINCT "sample_barcode"
        FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
        WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
        LIMIT 1
      )
ORDER BY "start_pos"
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries gradually expose the structure and contents of the copy‑number segment data needed before undertaking cytoband‑level CNV classification.
